local.properties
.gradle/
build/
# brain.db (~2.3MB) is deliberately COMMITTED, not ignored.
#
# It is nominally a build artefact of scripts/export_mobile_bundle.py, but that
# script reads data/tenants/<t>/embeddings/*.npy, tabular.duckdb and a graphml,
# and none of data/ is tracked. So nothing outside one laptop can rebuild it,
# and a CI-built APK without it installs and then answers nothing -- 13MB of
# shell. Committing it is what makes the cloud artifact demoable.
#
# Safe to commit: the student records in it are curated synthetic data authored
# for RAG evaluation, not real people.
#
# The ~23MB embedder under minilm/ stays out. Without it the app falls back to
# keyword-only retrieval, which it already handles and says so in the UI, and
# every records question still answers exactly as it does locally.
# ~90MB embedder, generated by scripts/export_minilm_onnx.py
app/src/main/assets/minilm/

# Upload signing key. A leak here is unrecoverable: Play associates the app
# with this certificate forever, so it must never be committed.
keystore/
# Suffixed variants too: a bare `keystore.properties` pattern does not match
# `keystore.properties.bak`/`.aside`, which is exactly how a signing password
# becomes stageable during routine editing.
keystore.properties*
